meta {
  name: 00. Init run id
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datapools?size=1
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

script:pre-request {
  bru.setVar('closureRunId', String(Date.now()));
}

tests {
  test("Reachable", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  **Scenario: a flow reaching an unreleased artifact must not be staged.**

  Builds a DataSet whose Pipeline writes into a POSTGIS sink bound to a DataStructure that was
  never released, then attempts to stage it. The backend walks out from the Pipeline over the
  references the model registry recorded and must refuse with **HTTP 422**
  (`urn:civitas:error:PIPELINE_CLOSURE_INVALID`), naming the pipeline and the artifact.

  A second DataStructure is released first, because the Pipeline needs an AVAILABLE DataSource and
  a DataSource can only be released once it is pinned to a released version.
}
